# Force LF in the working tree for every text file, regardless of any
# user/system core.autocrlf setting. Added 2026-09-05 after the working
# tree flipped to CRLF across the whole repo mid-session (Git for
# Windows' default install sets core.autocrlf=true system-wide, at
# C:\Program Files\Git\etc\gitconfig -- neither this repo's local config
# nor the user's global config had ever overridden it). Without this
# file, that default is one `git checkout`/`git reset --hard`/`git stash
# pop` away from rewriting every tracked file's line endings again,
# turning any future small change into a repo-wide diff that buries the
# real edit and makes `git blame`/`git log -p` useless.
* text=auto eol=lf
